---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
// Published Aug 2026. JMP designation = NMTC rural mobilization gap
// (sole-authored, clean identification, public replication repo); swapping
// the JMP is a one-block edit in the "Job market paper" section.
---
<Base
  title="Job market"
  description="Ian Helfrich is on the 2026-27 economics job market. Applied econometrics, international trade, spatial and high-dimensional methods. Ph.D. in Economics, Georgia Institute of Technology, 2024."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Job market candidate · AEA cycle 2026-27</span>
    <h1>On the 2026-27 economics job market.</h1>
    <p class="kicker">
      Applied econometrician working on spatial and high-dimensional methods,
      economic networks, and international trade. Ph.D. in Economics, Georgia
      Institute of Technology, 2024, with a doctoral minor in quantitative
      psychology.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/cv/helfrich-cv-july-2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download CV (PDF)</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="mailto:ianthelfrich@gmail.com?subject=Faculty%20search%20inquiry">Email Ian</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/research">Research</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="cycle-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">The cycle</span>
        <h2 id="cycle-title">Where the market clock stands.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The AEA 2026-27 cycle against today's date. The cursor is live; everything else is the calendar. Available for interviews through the signal window and at ASSA, in person or remote.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cyc-wrap">
      <svg id="cyc" viewBox="0 0 1000 150" role="img" aria-label="Timeline of the AEA 2026-27 job market cycle with a marker at today's date"></svg>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="facts-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">At a glance</span>
        <h2 id="facts-title">Candidate facts.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The short version committees need first; the full record sits one click away on the research, teaching, and CV pages.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid">
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Fields</h3>
        <p>Primary: applied econometrics, international trade, spatial and urban economics. Secondary: economic networks, labor and AI, policy evaluation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Education</h3>
        <p>Ph.D. Economics, Georgia Institute of Technology, 2024. M.S. GIS&amp;T, Georgia Tech, 2022. M.S. Economics, Georgia Tech, 2019. M.A. Economics, Indiana University, 2018.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Advisors</h3>
        <p>Dr. Tibor Besedes and Dr. Usha Nair-Reichert, Georgia Institute of Technology. References and letters are available on request.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Availability</h3>
        <p>Applying through AEA JOE this cycle. Available for interviews through the December signal window and at ASSA in January 2027, in person or remote.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="jmp-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Job market paper</span>
        <h2 id="jmp-title">The rural mobilization gap in U.S. place-based tax credit.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Sole-authored. Working paper, 2026. Replication code and viewer are public.</p>
    </div>
    <p>
      The paper decomposes the rural-versus-urban private-leverage gap in the
      U.S. New Markets Tax Credit using Community Development Entity fixed
      effects, on a project-level panel linking every Qualified Equity
      Investment from FY2001 to FY2022 to its issuing intermediary. The raw
      rural gap of &minus;0.262 falls to &minus;0.047 (p = 0.64) once CDE
      identity enters the model: 82.2 percent of the apparent rural penalty is
      between-intermediary selection. A Chetty-Kleven style bunching test shows
      the 20 percent non-metro mandate does not bind in cumulative-deployment
      data. The decomposition moves the policy target upstream, from rural
      project markets to the CDFI Fund rules that decide which intermediaries
      receive allocation authority.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/research/helfrich-2026-nmtc-rural-gap">Read the record</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/ihelfrich/us-nmtc-viewer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Replication code + viewer</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="papers-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Selected research</span>
        <h2 id="papers-title">The wider program.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Nine working papers and preprints, spanning applied trade measurement, optimal transport theory, and labor. Full list on the research page.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="h-row-list">
      <li class="h-row">
        <div class="h-row-meta">With Shane Vardanyan · working paper · 2026</div>
        <h3 class="h-row-title"><a href="/research/helfrich-vardanyan-2026-ai-entry-level-labor">AI and the entry-level labor market</a></h3>
        <p class="h-row-summary">Continuous-exposure event study and triple difference on generative-AI exposure and early-career U.S. employment, on CPS microdata.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="h-row">
        <div class="h-row-meta">With Elizaveta Gonchar · working paper · 2026</div>
        <h3 class="h-row-title"><a href="/research/gonchar-helfrich-2026-effective-distance-panel">Effective distance: a satellite-calibrated bilateral trade-cost panel, 2000-2024</a></h3>
        <p class="h-row-summary">A global, time-varying, multi-modal effective-distance panel, validated in structural gravity with three counterfactuals.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="h-row">
        <div class="h-row-meta">With Elizaveta Gonchar · SSRN 5202676 · 2025</div>
        <h3 class="h-row-title"><a href="/research/gonchar-helfrich-2025-spotlight">Trade in the spotlight: nightlights and population-weighted distance</a></h3>
        <p class="h-row-summary">Gravity estimates with population-weighted geodesic distance and VIIRS nightlights.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="h-row">
        <div class="h-row-meta">Sole-authored · SSRN 4772016 · 2024</div>
        <h3 class="h-row-title"><a href="/research/helfrich-2024-ssrn-4772016">A unifying framework for economic equilibrium and optimal transport in infinite-dimensional Hilbert spaces</a></h3>
        <p class="h-row-summary">Equilibrium as optimal transport on Hilbert spaces: existence, uniqueness, and prices as gradients of convex potentials.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="teaching-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Teaching</span>
        <h2 id="teaching-title">Instructor of record, and a public teaching stack.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Georgia Tech Graduate TA of the Year, 2023.</p>
    </div>
    <p>
      Instructor of record for three semesters at Georgia Tech (economics and
      policy, principles of microeconomics), graduate TA for undergraduate
      economics, graduate econometrics, and ECE signal processing, and roughly
      1,200 hours of independent instruction with 450+ students. Builder of
      open teaching sites used in real courses: Stats Lab, Inference Lab,
      Pictures of Inference, and course studios for USC Price and UC Berkeley
      syllabi. Teaching evaluations are available with the packet.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button secondary" href="/teaching">Teaching portfolio</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-panel">
    <span class="section-label">For hiring committees</span>
    <h2>The full packet, on request.</h2>
    <p>
      CV, job market paper, research and teaching statements, evaluations, and
      reference letters. Email and they arrive the same day.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="mailto:ianthelfrich@gmail.com?subject=Faculty%20search%20inquiry">Email Ian</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/cv/helfrich-cv-july-2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the CV (PDF)</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  // The cycle instrument: the AEA 2026-27 calendar drawn to scale, with a
  // live cursor at today. The only computed element is the cursor; the only
  // signal-blue element is the cursor. Everything else is ink on the axis.
  const svg = document.getElementById("cyc");
  if (svg) {
    const NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg";
    const T0 = new Date("2026-08-01T00:00:00").getTime();
    const T1 = new Date("2027-03-01T00:00:00").getTime();
    const L = 14, R = 986, AX = 108;
    const x = (d: string | number) =>
      L + ((typeof d === "number" ? d : new Date(d + "T12:00:00").getTime()) - T0) / (T1 - T0) * (R - L);
    const el = (tag: string, attrs: Record<string, string>, text?: string) => {
      const n = document.createElementNS(NS, tag);
      for (const k in attrs) n.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);
      if (text) n.textContent = text;
      svg.appendChild(n);
      return n;
    };
    const MONO = "font: 520 10.5px var(--ih-mono);";
    const band = (d0: string, d1: string, y: number, label: string) => {
      el("rect", { x: String(x(d0)), y: String(y), width: String(x(d1) - x(d0)), height: "16",
        rx: "3", fill: "rgba(17,17,19,0.07)", stroke: "rgba(17,17,19,0.28)", "stroke-width": "0.6" });
      el("text", { x: String(x(d0) + 5), y: String(y + 11.5), fill: "#3d3d42", style: MONO }, label);
    };
    // axis + month ticks
    el("line", { x1: String(L), y1: String(AX), x2: String(R), y2: String(AX), stroke: "#111113", "stroke-width": "1" });
    const months = ["2026-08-01","2026-09-01","2026-10-01","2026-11-01","2026-12-01","2027-01-01","2027-02-01","2027-03-01"];
    const names = ["Aug","Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec","Jan 27","Feb",""];
    months.forEach((m, i) => {
      const X = x(m);
      el("line", { x1: String(X), y1: String(AX - 4), x2: String(X), y2: String(AX + 4), stroke: "#898781", "stroke-width": "1" });
      if (names[i]) el("text", { x: String(X + 4), y: String(AX + 18), fill: "#898781", style: MONO }, names[i]);
    });
    band("2026-08-01", "2027-01-31", 30, "JOE listings open · Aug 1 to Jan 31");
    band("2026-10-01", "2026-11-30", 58, "deadline cluster · Oct to Nov");
    band("2026-12-01", "2026-12-15", 58, "");
    el("text", { x: String(x("2026-12-01")), y: "53", fill: "#3d3d42", style: MONO }, "signals · early Dec");
    // ASSA marker
    const ax2 = x("2027-01-03");
    el("path", { d: `M ${ax2} ${AX - 9} l 5 6 l -5 6 l -5 -6 z`, fill: "#111113" });
    el("text", { x: String(ax2 + 8), y: String(AX - 8), fill: "#3d3d42", style: MONO }, "ASSA · Jan 2027");
    // today: the one live element
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now >= T0 && now <= T1) {
      const X = x(now);
      el("line", { x1: String(X), y1: "22", x2: String(X), y2: String(AX + 6), stroke: "#2852e8", "stroke-width": "1.6" });
      const d = new Date();
      const lbl = `today · ${d.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric" })}`;
      const anchor = X > R - 120 ? "end" : "start";
      el("text", { x: String(X + (anchor === "end" ? -6 : 6)), y: "18", fill: "#2852e8",
        "text-anchor": anchor, style: MONO }, lbl);
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  .cyc-wrap {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    border: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 19, 0.12);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem 0.3rem;
  }
  .cyc-wrap svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
</style>
